## Code, knowledge and tools (kb)

Use the {{project_name}} KB at `{{kb_path}}` through `{{kb}}` for code lookups,
feature documentation, obligations and checks, instead of choosing between grep, file
search and code-graph tools. Skills: `{{agents_skill_path}}` (commands and answers),
`{{skills_dir}}/kb-change/SKILL.md` (changing code), `{{skills_dir}}/kb-review/SKILL.md`,
`{{skills_dir}}/kb-document/SKILL.md`. Any core below is valid only while its receipt
matches the selected snapshot; if that proof fails, use full current context and repair the
integration before reusing the core.
{{core_lines}}
Locate code with `{{kb}} sym`, `{{kb}} callers`, `{{kb}} impact <symbol>{{snapshot_arg}}` and `{{kb}} find`. Before the
first edit, read `{{kb}} doc <path>{{snapshot_arg}}` and request

    {{kb}} context --intent implement --task "<task>" --path <file> --skill-protocol {{skill_protocol}}{{snapshot_arg}}{{core_arg}}

(`--intent review --changed --base <target>` for a review). Apply all mandatory knowledge;
resolve missing scope and conflicts. Before finishing, run `{{kb}} check --base <target>{{snapshot_arg}}` and
`{{kb}} impact --base <target> --working-tree{{snapshot_arg}}`; update the
documentation in the same change when behavior changed. Answers are bounded and name their
source; acceptance of knowledge requires review and merge into the approved ref.

After compaction, hand-off or a new session request full context again. Only use a core
receipt after reading its source above; stale or missing installation evidence must be
repaired.

Managed by `{{kb}} integrate`; edit the KB and regenerate instead of this block.
